   "definitions": "per primary step, exact interval of the pre->post CHORD with cylinder intersect ellipsoid. The chord is not the path followed: multiple scattering displaces the post-step point sideways, so lengths in Z are chord lengths and their error is reported, not zero: max_lat_mm = largest lateral displacement over all primary steps (diagnostic); max_lat_z_mm / sum_lat_z_mm = largest / summed lateral displacement over the steps near Z (chord meets both primitives grown by near_margin_m); sum_lat_z_mm is a scale of the error of the chord lengths in Z, not a bound. crossed = some step longer than 2 eps inside Z with positive length inside Z shrunk by eps (so crossed = 1 implies n_steps_z >= 1); graze = touches Z grown by eps away from both step ends; lz_true = chord length x StepLength/|chord|; length split by the pre-step material; e_in/e_out interpolated along the chord with the step's [E_post, E_pre] bracket",
